Description: export the replicant factory symbols from the executable
 The Deskbar resolves a tray item by loading the provider image named in
 the archive's "add_on" string and looking up instantiate_deskbar_item
 and the view's Instantiate(BMessage*). A plain executable keeps those
 symbols in .symtab only, which the loader cannot see, so the replicant
 would come back grey. Link with -rdynamic so the factory symbols reach
 the dynamic symbol table - the same export contract the tree's own
 replicant apps get from the runnable-add-on link rule, which the
 Makefile-Engine does not implement.
Author: Dario Casalinuovo <b.vitruvio@gmail.com>
Forwarded: not-needed

--- a/Makefile
+++ b/Makefile
@@ -108,7 +108,7 @@
 COMPILER_FLAGS =
 
 #	specify additional linker flags
-LINKER_FLAGS =
+LINKER_FLAGS = -rdynamic
 
 #	specify the version of this particular item
 #	(for example, -app 3 4 0 d 0 -short 340 -long "340 "`echo -n -e '\302\251'`"1999 GNU GPL")
